#!/bin/sh
# ascend's pre-push gate -- the shim.
#
# This file is the SOURCE of the hook. It is not the file git runs.
#
# WHY THERE IS A SECOND HOOK AT ALL. `asc-09wx.14`'s third cut lets a commit run only the tests its
# staged paths can reach (`scripts/gate-scope.mjs`), because most commits change one package and the
# whole suite is minutes of the gate's cost. That cut is paid for HERE: a push runs the gate with
# every cut disabled, so the full suite and `align check` are in the loop before the work leaves this
# machine. A commit proves what it touched; a push proves the repository.
#
# WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT DUPLICATED. There is no second step list. This hook runs the same
# `scripts/gate.mjs` the commit runs, with `ASCEND_PRECOMMIT_FULL=1` -- the escape hatch that already
# meant "run everything, and also `align check`". One runner, one definition of the steps, and a cut
# can never leave a check unwired at push time, because the push path does not know about cuts.
#
# `ASCEND_GATE_HOOK` is what the runner prints in front of each line. Without it a push would talk
# about pre-commit, and the reader would be told the wrong moment is failing.
#
# THE THREE INVARIANTS ARE THE SAME ONES, and they are not restated here in weaker words -- see
# `.githooks/pre-commit`, where each was measured:
#
#   1. Never terminate the shell above beads' block. This hook has one too: `.beads/hooks/pre-push`
#      exists today as beads' own template, and the installer splices this above it. A bare `exit 0`
#      would make that block unreachable while `bd hooks list` still reported health.
#   2. The work runs in a SUBSHELL, so `set -eu` and `cd` cannot leak into beads' block.
#   3. The subshell is a STANDALONE command whose status is captured, never the condition of an `if`
#      -- POSIX suppresses `set -e` inside an `if` condition, which is the false green measured in
#      `.githooks/pre-commit` (suite red, gate green) and the reason the capture is written this way.
#
# A FAILING PUSH IS BLOCKED, and that is the point: TASKS.md non-negotiable #5 forbids `--no-verify`,
# and a suite that is red at push time is a suite the commit's cut did not run. The remedy is to fix
# the tree, not to bypass the hook.
#
# COST. This is the expensive path, and it is on purpose: the whole suite plus a repo scan. What it is
# NOT is once per push, and this paragraph said exactly that until it was measured. Git runs this hook
# once per `git push` COMMAND it is handed -- one push carrying two refs is still one run, and two
# pushes are two -- and `but push` pushes a stack one branch at a time. So a stack is gated once per
# BRANCH, on an index that does not move between them: measured 2026-10-14, one `but push` of a
# two-branch stack ran this gate twice, 302.4 s and 259.0 s of the 568 s the push took (`dogfood/0099`).
#
# What makes the repeats affordable is Cut 4. The second run computes the same tree, and
# `ASCEND_PRECOMMIT_FULL` no longer puts `scripts/gate-memo.mjs` out of reach -- a PUSH's record clears
# a push's bar (`requiredOf` in `scripts/gate.mjs`), so the second is answered rather than paid for. A
# record a COMMIT left still cannot answer here, and that is the bar: it is the one step only a run
# with no cuts plans, and no commit-level run ever takes `align check`.

(
  set -eu
  ROOT="$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)"
  cd "$ROOT"
  ASCEND_GATE_HOOK=pre-push ASCEND_PRECOMMIT_FULL=1 node scripts/gate.mjs
)
status=$?

if [ "$status" -ne 0 ]; then
  echo "[pre-push] ascend gate FAILED (exit $status) -- push blocked" >&2
  exit 1
fi

echo "[pre-push] ascend gate ok"

# WHICH COMMITS THIS CHECKOUT HAS NEVER JUDGED, said and not enforced.
#
# A commit can exist that no gate has read: `git commit` runs the hook, but a tool that creates
# commits through its own library does not, and GitButler did exactly that for a year (`asc-rzhr`,
# `dogfood/0095`). Until `scripts/gate-coverage.mjs` existed, nothing here could even name such a
# commit. This is the moment the list is worth printing: the work is about to leave the machine. It
# WARNS rather than blocks, deliberately, because a commit whose content was edited again in the
# worktree, or which another applied branch also changed, is not a commit this hook can prove anything
# about -- and a hook that blocked on a maybe would be bypassed within a week.
#
# `|| true` and a subshell, for the reason the gate above is a subshell: this must never change the
# push's status, and `cd` must not leak into beads' block below.
#
# SKIPPED UNDER `ASCEND_GATE_NO_RECORD`, which is how `packages/cli/test/dev-hooks.test.ts` runs the
# hooks. That fixture runs in this repository, so the query would read the real log and the real
# commits six times per suite for a warning no assertion reads -- real work done for a fixture.
if [ -z "${ASCEND_GATE_NO_RECORD:-}" ]; then
  (
    cd "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)"
    node scripts/ungated-commits.mjs --warn >&2
  ) || true
fi
